From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:47:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: t8132-platform-data: keep the J713's USB
 AON hand-over to the J713

t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi marks ps_atc0_usb_aon and ps_atc1_usb_aon
apple,inherited-on: the J713's loader hands them over on, and Linux may
read but not switch them. The built-in policy includes that file for
every T8132 machine on the firmware path, so these two entries would
also take the switch away from the J604, whose tree lets an idle USB-C
port's AON domain power down.

Name the J713 on both, as the J713's ACIO power states already do.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
index 90f6cf3c7a..309733a8d2 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/t8132-platform-data.dts
@@ -63,6 +63,15 @@ &ps_atc1_cio_usb {
 	apple,policy-machine = "apple,j713";
 };
 
+/* The J713 hands over its two USB AON domains on; other boards own theirs. */
+&ps_atc0_usb_aon {
+	apple,policy-machine = "apple,j713";
+};
+
+&ps_atc1_usb_aon {
+	apple,policy-machine = "apple,j713";
+};
+
 &mcc {
 	apple,boot-dma-devices = <&pmp>;
 };
